<p class="eyebrow">Lectures, webinars and workshops</p><h1>Teaching</h1><p class="lede">I teach computational design and AI workflows through practical tools, inspectable examples and work that participants can keep developing.</p>
<p>Alongside product and design work, I give lectures, webinars and workshops for international design communities, including DesignMorphine and DigitalFUTURES.</p>
<h2>Topics</h2><ul><li>Parametric and procedural design: connecting design intent to editable systems.</li><li>AI workflows: defining inputs, checking outputs and making a procedure reusable.</li><li>Spatial tools and interactive 3D: moving between models, interfaces and buildable work.</li></ul>
<h2>Materials and experiments</h2><p>The <a href="/ai-work">AI Work archive</a> documents practical tests. The <a href="/projects">project index</a> links to the tools and technical sources behind this approach.</p>
